+# Patch 0030: in-app help, pages 7 to 9 (B7)
+
+Items: the 0030 pages from the B7 page plan. Status: `[x]` done and tested in my sandbox, `[ ]` needs you.
+
+## What you asked for
+- Continue B7 with the next three pages. Small chunks, three pages per patch, each planned in the progress doc and ticked as it is done. B6 (training mode) comes after this.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Re-cloned the repo (latest is "Docs Part 2", which contains 0029) and re-read `DEV_NOTES.md` and `docs/PROGRESS.md`.
+2. [x] Read the code behind each page before writing it: `src/screens/Lookup.tsx`, `src/lib/lookup.ts`, `src/lib/posLock.ts`, `src/lib/staffAuth.ts`, `src/lib/screensaver.ts` (the five-minute card rule), `src/screens/SavedCarts.tsx`, `src/lib/savedOps.ts`, the saved cart parts of `src/lib/sync.ts`, `mergeCarts`, `SaveCartSheet`, `CustomerSheet`, `src/screens/Customers.tsx`, `src/lib/shopify/customers.ts`, `orderModel.ts`, `Receipt.tsx`.
+3. [x] `help/sales/lookup-tiles.md`: Lock POS (what blocks it and why), Price check (price, compare-at, deals as a hint), Stock check (totals), scan messages. Two flowcharts.
+4. [x] `help/sales/saved-carts.md`: saving, opening, merging, Assign (a label only), delete and swipe, sharing through Shopify every 25 seconds, offline behaviour. One flowchart.
+5. [x] `help/sales/customers.md`: attaching, searching, creating, the Customers list, why a customer made on another register may not show until an import or Search Shopify. One flowchart.
+6. [x] `npm run help:build` (9 pages, no problems) and `help/help.json` rewritten.
+7. [x] Tests: the existing help tests (45) pass, including the citation check. No new tests: these are pages only.
+8. [x] `docs/PROGRESS.md`: patch log row, the 0030 pages ticked, B7c no longer called 0030, and a new "page update owed" line for `sales/cart-and-prices` (A16 is now built).
+9. [ ] You: N21 now also covers these three pages.
+
+## Things I noticed while reading the code (not changed here)
+- More ▸ **Lock register** locks without the "card payment waiting" check that the Lock POS tile does. A card payment can therefore be left waiting behind the Sign in screen. The page describes both as they are.
+- `locked_by` and `locked_at` exist on the saved cart definition but nothing writes them, so two registers editing one saved cart is last write wins.
+- **Assign** on a saved cart is only a label. Nothing filters or notifies by it.
+- The customer list on a register is only refreshed by Import from Shopify, not by the background check.
